{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Controls"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Layout","anchor":"Layout","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Text input is based on several configurable UI elements:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"label"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": It is used to describe the purpose of the input."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In some UI contexts, especially when space is limited or when the input is part of a compact layout (search bars, filters, inline forms), the label can be hidden."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However, hiding the label should only be done if the purpose of the input remains clear thanks to a placeholder or contextual icon"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and if the label is still accessible to screen readers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Hiding a label is a design choice that must balance visual simplicity and clarity of intent, without compromising inclusiveness or form guidance."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"placeholder"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": if the text of the text input is empty a placeholder provides a hint or guidance inside the field to suggest expected input."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A prefix and a suffix can be added to give more context."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"leading icon"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": it helps indicate the purpose of the input (magnifying glass for search, envelope for email, phone device for phone number)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only use a leading icon if it adds clear functional or contextual value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trailing action"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": it is used to provide actions related to the field: clear input, toggle password visibility, open a date picker, etc."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Can also indicate status or feedback (error checkmark, loading spinner)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Outlined style","anchor":"Outlined-style","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", the input is with a subtle background fill and invisible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"outlined","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", the text input is a minimalist design with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a header (search field)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["   \/\/ An outlined text input","   OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, isOutlined: true)","","   \/\/ With a localizable and a bundle","   OUDSTextInput(LocalizedStringKey(\"label_wording\"), bundle: Bundle.module, text: $text)"]},{"text":"Rounded layout","anchor":"Rounded-layout","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text input can have rounded layouts to be favored in more emotional, immersive contexts or those tied to specific visual identities.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For standard or business-oriented journeys, keep the default corners.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This evolution addresses the need for flexibility in adapting the design to some brand contexts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To activate the rounded corner behavior, set to true the ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasRoundedTextInputs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tuning","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in your theme configuration (if the theme exposes this property at init).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Some themes do not have this flexibility like ","type":"text"},{"code":"SoshTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"WireframeTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Status","anchor":"Status","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Five status are proposed for all layouts:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default (by default)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Default neutral appearance, whether empty or filled."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It allows users to click, focus, and type freely without restrictions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"error"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": The "},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expected formatting. It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input. The error messages replaces the helper text."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"loading"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": The "},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state indicates that the system is processing or retrieving data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"related to the text entered. A progress indicator appears to inform the user that an action is in progress."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"readOnly"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" :The"},{"code":"readOnly","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", lets the text visible but not editable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disabled"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": In "},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" status, the field is non-interactive and grayed out to indicate it cannot be changed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Note the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View.disabled()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Helpers","anchor":"Helpers","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":":  A supporting text conveys additional information about the input field,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as how it will be used. It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper link"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": If the helper text is not sufficient, it’s possible to offer the user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an additional help link (the link can be external or open a modal)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Accessibility considerations","anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default no haptics are done by the component for the trailing action.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However you should think about cases wher you will have to make the devices vibrates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can refer to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-haptics"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Mandatory field indication","anchor":"Mandatory-field-indication","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields are mandatory” at the top of your formular.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Do not use an asterisk at the end of each field label, nor the word “mandatory.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields marked with an * are mandatory” at the top of your formular.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use an asterisk (*) at the end of each mandatory field label, and ensures this is well vocalized.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"UI rendering of the asterisk must be done with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"bold font weight","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"negative content color","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (red on light backgrounds).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the mention “(optional)” at the end of each optional field label. Note that this rule is not systematic, it remains an option, to be used if needed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If there is only one field in the formular, or if the mandatory nature is obvious (such as login\/password),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no mention is necessary since the fields are essential to the formular’s functionality.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Rich text","anchor":"Rich-text","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No other text styles should be used.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Code samples","anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ The text to display and edit","    @State var text: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ Empty text and no placeholder","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text)","","    \/\/ Empty text with placeholder and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\")","","    \/\/ Empty text with prefix and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, prefix: \"Distance\", suffix: \"km\")","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon for more context","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(systemName: \"envelope\")))","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon displayed as raw image (not tinted)","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Brand\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_brand\"), renderingMode: .original))","","    \/\/ Flip the leading icon for RTL layouts using OUDSImage.flipped","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))","","    \/\/ Add a trailing button with local image named \"ic_cross\" for additional action","    let trailingAction = OUDSTextInput.TrailingAction(image: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_cross\")), actionHint: \"Delete\") { text = \"\" }","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, trailingAction: trailingAction)","","    \/\/ With helper text","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\",","                  text: $text,","                  placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\",","                  suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  helperText: \"The email will be automatically completed with @orange.com\")","","    \/\/ With helper link","    @Environment(\\.openURL) private var openUrl","","    let helperLink = OUDSTextInput.HelperLink(text: \"Helper Link\") {","       openUrl.callAsFunction(url)","    }","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, placeholder: \"Placeholder\", helperLink: helperLink)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to flip your leading icon for RTL, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"flipped","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSImage"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["    @Environment(\\.layoutDirection) var layoutDirection","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))"]},{"text":"Design documentation","anchor":"Design-documentation","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-text-input"}]},{"text":"Themes rendering","anchor":"Themes-rendering","type":"heading","level":2},{"text":"Orange","anchor":"Orange","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Orange"}]},{"text":"Orange Compact","anchor":"Orange-Compact","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_OrangeCompact"}]},{"text":"Sosh","anchor":"Sosh","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Sosh"}]},{"text":"Wireframe","anchor":"Wireframe","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Wireframe"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Version","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.4.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Since","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"0.20.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSTextInput"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OUDSTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false}],"title":"OUDSTextInput","externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents13OUDSTextInputV","roleHeading":"Structure"},"abstract":[{"text":"Text input is a UI element that allows to enter, edit, or select single-line textual data.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Text input is one of the most fundamental form elements used to capture user input such as names, emails, passwords, or search queries.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides a visual and interactive affordance for text entry while supporting labels, placeholders, icons, descriptions, and validation feedback.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/Helperlink","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/TrailingAction"]},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/init(_:tableName:bundle:text:placeholder:prefix:suffix:leadingImage:trail